MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_001: Gosh, the shops here have such a nice selection.\nMaybe I should buy something.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_002: Well hello, young lady. Admiring our\nwonderful wares?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_003: We have all manner of outfit accessories, earrings,\nhair clips. Color-coordinate as much as you like.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_004: What? I don't need those. And I'm a boy, you jerk!\nI'm gonna leave.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_005: "Little lady," he says. Pah! While I'm here wearing\nthese clothes and everything.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_006: You try going undercover and your disguise gets\nblown like nothing.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_007: Sirocco did say people could tell. Maybe it really is\nthat bad...
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_008: Huh, there's Peter. Is he looking for someone?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_009: Mu! I'm glad to see you. Can you come with me for\na minute?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_010: A pregnant lady with big bags sat down and can't get\nback up. I need a strong man to help.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_011: Oh—sure! A strong man, that's me.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_012: Whew. We got her back home.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_013: Yeah. I'm glad she's safe and sound.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_014: Thanks, Mu. I couldn't have helped her by myself.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_015: You carried so many bags. You're really strong.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_016: I am, aren't I? That's 'cause I'm a man. With muscles!
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_017: You need a man to help—I'm who you call. I pick\nstuff up, and...other things men do!
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_018: Yeah, of course. If anything comes up, I'll be sure to\nask. See you later.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_019: Peter hasn't figured out my disguise. I guess it's a\ncoincidence the shopkeeper saw through me.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_020: Sirocco, he's an expert on girls, in a weird way.\nOf course he'd know.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_C_021: OK! No need to go doubting myself. That's a relief.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_001: That was delicious. We have to eat there again\nsometime, Mu.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_002: Yeah! It's nice to kick back and enjoy a meal\nfor once. Thanks.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_003: Don't mention it. You're easy to be around.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_004: And not just for the everyday stuff, but in battle too.\nI feel stronger when you're with me, Mu.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_005: It doesn't feel quite right when we're on\ndifferent sides.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_006: Yeah, we work well together. Like that time we both\ntook out enemies in each other's blind spots!
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_007: Hehe. Yeah, I've got your back. That's how guys\nroll. I don't have much, but I've got good eyes.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_008: Yep—how guys roll! You and me, Peter, we got each\nother's backs.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_009: Great! Oh, hang on. I think I'm missing my coin\npurse. I'll take a look around. You go on ahead.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_010: Off he goes. "How guys roll," huh? Guess I really do\nhave him fooled...
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_011: I was pretending as a way to protect myself, and\nPeter seems safe, so—maybe it's OK if I tell him?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_012: Sorry to keep you, Mu. I got it. Some random, kind\nstranger found it.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_013: Oh! Hey. Glad you found it so quickly.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_014: Yeah, and the person who picked it up was the lady\nwe helped before. Can you believe it?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_015: Small world! That's a miracle.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_016: It's probably because you're so nice! You treat\neveryone right, whether they're a boy or a girl.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_017: But that's the way it should be, right? It doesn't\nmatter if you're helping a man or a woman.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_018: Right! Right. It really feels like I can tell him...
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_019: I guess maybe that's not always true for me, though.\nI don't treat everyone the same way.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_020: When I'm with a girl I like, it's different. I'm just\nso awkward.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_021: When I'm with a girl I like, it's different, especially\nif we're trying to work through an argument.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_023: Wha?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_024: Hey, keep that to yourself, OK? I shouldn't have\nblurted that out, but you're so easy to talk to.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_025: Right. Sounds good. Feel free to tell me all about any\ngirls you like.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_026: That's what guys do. They have...guy talk.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_027: Really? Then I guess we've got a lot to talk about.\nAnd feel free to share about yourself too, Mu.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_B_028: I will... If I can.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_001: Bull's–eye. Yep, that'll work.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_002: Hey, good aim! I don't think I could've hit the target\nin the dark.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_003: Aah! Mu! How long have you been there?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_004: Since around when you got three in a row.\nYou didn't notice me, so I just stayed and watched.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_005: You look so cool and tough when you've got an\narrow nocked!
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_006: Th-thank you... But next time, don't sneak up on me.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_007: C'mon, you're not even looking at me. And you're\nbeing so quiet. We've talked a ton of times!
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_008: It's different when it's just you and me, at night.\nI used to think we were two buddies hanging out.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_009: You really never caught on, Peter! Other guys had\nme figured out.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_010: I truly am sorry that I lied to you. I wanted to\ntell you, I really did...
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_011: but it had gone on so long, I was scared you would\nhate me for deceiving you.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_012: I don't feel deceived. Listen, you're my friend, aren't\nyou, Mu?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_013: And I said it myself. Man or woman, it really\nshouldn't matter.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_014: I enjoyed the time we spent together, Mu. I hope our\nfriendship wasn't a lie.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_015: Aw, Peter...
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_016: So let's keep being friends, the way we were.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_017: Oh. That's what you want to do? I'm disappointed.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_018: Wh-what do you mean?
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_019: Well, you said it was "different" around some girls.\nI want that! I want you to notice me.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_020: "Notice" you? But I already...
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_021: No need to say anything. This is plenty for me\nright now.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_022: But I should warn you—I'm very, very stubborn.\nI hardly ever admit defeat.
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_023: I'm tenacious, just like my mom, and I'm gonna wear\nyou down. Be prepared!
MID_SE_Pet_Moo_A_024: Prepared? This is way more stressful than fighting.